  nonce: 146c  # 146c
  message: "[REVIEW 2026-11-15: PARTLY DONE] 2026-11-15, dev e2b6ab8096, scheme v14. Fixture: bash still emits `bash:redirect:0-0:>:external_symbol` (bash.py:1577-1578); cpp emits `cpp:module-set-<hash>:0-0:printf` with a top-level `module_sets` table; swift local-receiver and objc in-repo-class calls land in `external`. WI-daruz (done, d71106555d, 2026-10-28) reclassified `redirect` from sentinel to namespace in module_key_axis.py (lines 176-192, 322-334); io_primitives/bash.yaml keys rows on `module: redirect` at :96 and :104. ADR-0051:134 still lists `redirect` as a sentinel and :181-186 still states the v9/v10 gate. Self-analysis extract: 28,474 of 94,310 external-symbol edges use the `external` slot, 161 `redirect`, 24 `module-set-`. Cohort re-measure not run. Full review: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/reports/WI-marok.md. No status or priority change made by this review."  # 146c
- op: discuss  # 68bc
  at: '2026-11-15T19:47:30Z'  # 68bc
  by: agent  # 68bc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 68bc
  clock: 8  # 68bc
  nonce: 68bc  # 68bc
  message: "[INVESTIGATION 2026-11-15, owner-requested; dev e2b6ab8096] (1) redirect. The registry classes bash's `redirect` as a namespace (module_key_axis.py:176-192 and :322-334) since WI-daruz-jivih-vumiz-vifub-hohah-kipir-horak-vojum (d71106555d, PR #1931, 2026-10-28). The ground: the 2026-09-01 audit kept it a sentinel with the written trigger \"any catalogue row whose module is literally redirect\", and io_primitives/bash.yaml has shipped such rows since 08-14 (:96 fs_write for > >| >>, :104 fs_read for <); taint branches on the `redirect.` prefix. The trigger was true when written, so the limb's premise (nothing keys on the slot) is false, and migrating the slot would remove the rows by which verify-claims sees a shell script's file reads and writes. RECOMMENDATION: drop the redirect limb; do not contest WI-daruz-jivih-vumiz-vifub-hohah-kipir-horak-vojum. The original complaint that '>' is \"not a call at all\" is about modelling a redirection as a calls edge, which is an edge-type question and not a module-key one; not filed. (2) module-set handle. Already ruled: owner 2026-10-23, INV-jahuf-zujit-numub-lotos-pubuk-rafuf-vovor-jipun (satisfied, scheme v12); the handle and the top-level module_sets table are in the spec (:1003-1009). (3) external. ADR-0051 section 3 calls uncertainty values \"non-conformant as identities while being the honest answer to the question\"; the registry calls `external` \"load-bearing as an admission\" (_UNRESOLVED_MODULE_PLACEHOLDERS_IO is shared by io_boundary and taint); WI-jokij-kanot-niril-tonom-jubuv-borom-jafin-pizok (open) is titled \"the external sentinel is the honest cell for untyped-receiver calls\". No record asks for its migration, and replacing a stated unknown with a guess is the opposite of what the placeholder is for. (4) ADR-0051 is out of date in three places: :133 describes the disjunction as cpp's comma-joined include set; :134 lists redirect as a sentinel; :181-186 states the v9/v10 gate and \"7.8% of shipped slots\". (5) Not measured: the 21-repo cohort. Today's self-analysis only: of 94,310 external-symbol edges, 28,474 use `external`, 161 `redirect`, 24 `module-set-`. WHAT REMAINS if the owner agrees: (a) the cohort re-measure, to learn whether any violator class is left after the objc, swift and cpp fixes; (b) the three ADR-0051 corrections; (c) one sentence in ADR-0051 recording that `external` and the module-set handle are legal uncertainty values. Proposed title: \"module-key step 7 residual: re-measure the cohort and bring ADR-0051 in line with the registry (redirect is a namespace, the disjunction is a module-set handle, external stays)\". No status, title or priority change made."  # 68bc
